\ Spitfire: the mission's briefing, between choosing a mission and flying
\ it. A map of the area from above: the coastlines and the lochs' shores,
\ the airfields and towns within it, the Spitfire's start and its heading,
\ the raid's start, track and target, the mission's target, a scale bar in
\ miles and the north mark; the map's square takes in every point the
\ mission names, with a margin, and at least 30 km across. Beside it the
\ particulars, read from the mission: the time of day and the moon, the
\ aircraft and its guns or cameras, the propeller, the boost, the start,
\ the weather and the opposition. Below them the mission's own briefing.
\ The chart N shows in flight is drawn from the same map in more detail.

16 constant map-left
32 constant map-top
288 constant map-size
332 constant particulars-left
410 constant values-left
214 constant values-width
332 constant briefing-top
0xff6040 constant raid-colour

\ the rectangle a map is drawn in, [ left top width height ]: the briefing's square, or the whole screen for the chart
[ map-left map-top map-size map-size ] constant briefing-sheet
[ 0 0 640 480 ] constant chart-sheet
variable sheet
briefing-sheet to sheet

: sheet! ( rectangle -- )
	| rectangle ^sheet |
	rectangle to sheet ;
0xffe080 constant heading-colour

\ a text broken at spaces into lines no wider than a width in pixels
: wrapped-lines ( text width -- lines )
	| text width |
	[ ] to lines
	"" to filling
	text " +" split to words
	0 words size 1 do k
		words k @i to word
		filling "" = if word else filling " " + word + then to candidate
		candidate text-width width > filling "" = not and if
			lines filling add-last! drop
			word to filling
		else
			candidate to filling
		then
	loop
	lines filling add-last! ;

\ metres as feet, to the nearest hundred
: hundreds-of-feet ( metres -- feet ) 3.28084 * 100 / round 100 * ;

\ the places marked on the map when they fall within it, each [ landmark name ]
: map-places ( -- places )
	[ [ :turnhouse "TURNHOUSE" ] [ :drem "DREM" ] [ :abbotsinch "ABBOTSINCH" ] [ :dalcross "DALCROSS" ]
	  [ :acklington "ACKLINGTON" ] [ :wick "WICK" ] [ :vaernes "VAERNES" ]
	  [ :edinburgh-castle "EDINBURGH" ] [ :glasgow-cathedral "GLASGOW" ] [ :greenock "GREENOCK" ]
	  [ :clydebank "CLYDEBANK" ] [ :tynemouth "TYNEMOUTH" ] [ :nidaros "TRONDHEIM" ]
	  [ :forth-bridge "FORTH BRIDGE" ] [ :farne-islands "FARNE ISLANDS" ] [ :inverness-castle "INVERNESS" ]
	  [ :narvik "NARVIK" ] [ :bardufoss "BARDUFOSS" ] [ :bjerkvik "BJERKVIK" ] [ :ankenes "ANKENES" ]
	  [ :marischal-college "ABERDEEN" ] [ :dyce "DYCE" ] [ :peterhead "PETERHEAD" ] [ :montrose "MONTROSE" ]
	  [ :montrose-air-station "RAF MONTROSE" ] [ :castletown "CASTLETOWN" ] [ :kirkwall "KIRKWALL" ]
	  [ :hatston "HATSTON" ] [ :skeabrae "SKEABRAE" ] [ :lyness "LYNESS" ] [ :lerwick "LERWICK" ]
	  [ :sumburgh "SUMBURGH" ] ] ;

\ the ground points a mission names, each [ x z ]: the start, the raid's start and target, the mission's target, the tug's start, the carrier
: mission-points ( mission -- points )
	| mission |
	mission@start first to start
	[ [ start first start 2 @i ] ] to points
	mission@raid to plan
	plan null? not if
		points [ plan@start first plan@start 2 @i ] add-last! drop
		points [ plan@target first plan@target 2 @i ] add-last! drop
	then
	mission :target null @or to target
	target null? not if
		target landmark-ground to place
		points [ place first place 2 @i ] add-last! drop
	then
	mission :tug-start null @or to tug-place
	tug-place null? not if points [ tug-place first tug-place 2 @i ] add-last! drop then
	mission :carrier null @or to carrier
	carrier null? not if points [ carrier@centre first carrier@centre 2 @i ] add-last! drop then
	points ;

\ the map's centre, metres east and north, and its scale, pixels a metre: the square round the mission's points with a 30% margin, at least 30 km across, fitted to the shorter side of the sheet in use
: map-frame ( mission -- frame )
	| mission |
	mission mission-points to points
	points ( point | point first ) map to xs
	points ( point | point second ) map to zs
	xs 1e12 ' min2 reduce to west
	xs -1e12 ' max2 reduce to east
	zs 1e12 ' min2 reduce to south
	zs -1e12 ' max2 reduce to north
	east west - north south - max2 2 / 1.3 * 15000 max2 to half-size
	{ :x west east + 2 / :z south north + 2 / :scale sheet 2 @i sheet 3 @i min2 2 / half-size / } ;

\ a ground point's place on the map, [ column row ]
: map-at ( frame x z -- column row )
	| frame x z |
	sheet spread to height to width to top to left
	left width 2 / + x frame@x - frame@scale * +
	top height 2 / + z frame@z - frame@scale * - ;

\ whether a map place lies within the map's rectangle, a margin inside it
: on-map? ( column row margin -- flag )
	| column row margin |
	sheet spread to height to width to top to left
	column left margin + >= column left width + margin - <= and
	row top margin + >= and row top height + margin - <= and ;

\ the shore lines as map segments, each [ x0 y0 x1 y1 ]: the coastlines, Norway's shores round Trondheim and Narvik and the lochs', each point kept 1.5 pixels or more from the last, a segment kept when an end lies within 50 pixels of the map
: map-lines ( frame -- segments )
	| frame |
	lochs keys ( key | lochs key @ :shores @ ) map [ ] ' concat reduce to loch-shores
	coastlines norway-shores concat narvik-shores concat loch-shores concat to shores
	[ ] to segments
	0 shores size 1 do k
		shores k @i to shore
		shore first spread frame -rot map-at to last-row to last-column
		1 shore size 1 do m
			shore m @i spread frame -rot map-at to row to column
			column last-column - sq row last-row - sq + 2.25 >= m shore size 1- = or if
				column row -50 on-map? last-column last-row -50 on-map? or if
					segments [ last-column last-row column row ] add-last! drop
				then
				column to last-column
				row to last-row
			then
		loop
	loop
	segments ;

\ the names already on the map, each the box it covers, [ left top right bottom ]
variable placed-labels
[ ] to placed-labels

\ whether a box overlaps any name already on the map
: label-clashes? ( left top right bottom -- flag )
	| left top right bottom |
	placed-labels ( box |
		left box 2 @i < right box first > and top box 3 @i < and bottom box second > and
	) filter size 0 > ;

\ where a mark's name goes: right of the mark, or left of it when the right side runs off the map or onto another name; null when both sides clash and the name may be left out, the right side when it may not
: place-label ( column row name gap required -- position )
	| column row name gap required ^placed-labels |
	name text-width to width
	row 6 - to top
	column gap + to right-left
	column gap - width - to left-left
	sheet first to sheet-left
	sheet first sheet 2 @i + to sheet-right
	right-left width + sheet-right 2 - <= right-left top right-left width + top 12 + label-clashes? not and if
		right-left to left
	else left-left sheet-left 2 + >= left-left top left-left width + top 12 + label-clashes? not and if
		left-left to left
	else required if
		right-left width + sheet-right 2 - <= if right-left else left-left then to left
	else
		null exit
	then then then
	placed-labels [ left top left width + top 12 + ] add-last! drop
	[ left top ] ;

\ a mark on the map with its name beside it, when within the map; a place whose name has no room is left out
: draw-map-mark ( column row name colour required -- )
	| column row name colour required |
	column row 4 on-map? not if exit then
	column row name 5 required place-label to position
	position null? if exit then
	column 1 - row 1 - 3 3 colour fill-span
	position spread name colour draw-text ;

\ a cross on the map with its name beside it, when within the map
: draw-map-cross ( column row name colour -- )
	| column row name colour |
	column row 6 on-map? not if exit then
	column 4 - row 4 - column 4 + row 4 + colour draw-segment
	column 4 - row 4 + column 4 + row 4 - colour draw-segment
	column row name 7 true place-label spread name colour draw-text ;

\ the scale bar: the longest of 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50 and 100 miles no longer than 90 pixels, under the map's lower left corner
: draw-scale-bar ( frame colour -- )
	| frame colour |
	[ 1 2 5 10 20 50 100 ] ( miles | miles 1609.34 * frame@scale * 90 <= ) filter to fitting
	fitting size 0 = if exit then
	fitting last to miles
	miles 1609.34 * frame@scale * to length
	sheet first 8 + to x
	sheet second sheet 3 @i + 10 - to y
	x y x length + y colour draw-segment
	x y 3 - x y 3 + colour draw-segment
	x length + y 3 - x length + y 3 + colour draw-segment
	x length + 6 + y 6 - miles 1 = if "1 MILE" else miles "{0} MILES" format then colour draw-text ;

\ the map: its square, the shores, the places, the raid's target, the mission's target, the scale and north; on the briefing also the start and its heading, the raid's start and track, the tug and the carrier, which in flight, the chart on the pilot's knee, would be out of date; whatever of the shores falls outside covered over by the screen's ground
: draw-briefing-map ( mission frame segments briefing -- )
	| mission frame segments briefing ^placed-labels |
	map-left map-top map-size map-size board-colour fill-span
	dial-ink 0.55 dimmed to shore-colour
	segments ( segment | segment spread shore-colour draw-segment ) each
	0 0 640 map-top wall-colour fill-span
	0 map-top map-size + 640 480 map-top - map-size - wall-colour fill-span
	0 map-top map-left map-size wall-colour fill-span
	map-left map-size + map-top 640 map-left - map-size - map-size wall-colour fill-span
	map-left map-top map-size map-size edge-colour outline
	[ ] to placed-labels
	mission@start first to start
	frame start first start 2 @i map-at to start-row to start-column
	briefing if
		mission@start second PI 180 / * to bearing
		start-column start-row start-column bearing sin 14 * + start-row bearing cos 14 * - heading-colour draw-segment
		start-column start-row 3 heading-colour fill-disc
	then
	mission@raid to plan
	plan null? not if
		frame plan@start first plan@start 2 @i map-at to raid-row to raid-column
		frame plan@target first plan@target 2 @i map-at to target-row to target-column
		briefing if raid-column raid-row target-column target-row raid-colour draw-segment then
		target-column target-row "TARGET" raid-colour draw-map-cross
		briefing if raid-column raid-row "RAID" raid-colour true draw-map-mark then
	then
	mission :aircraft :fighter @or :reconnaissance = if
		mission@target landmark-ground to place
		frame place first place 2 @i map-at "TIRPITZ" raid-colour draw-map-cross
	then
	mission :tug-start null @or to tug-place
	tug-place null? not briefing and if frame tug-place first tug-place 2 @i map-at "TUG" dial-ink true draw-map-mark then
	mission :carrier null @or to carrier
	carrier null? not briefing and if frame carrier@centre first carrier@centre 2 @i map-at "GLORIOUS" dial-ink true draw-map-mark then
	briefing if start-column start-row "YOU" 6 true place-label spread "YOU" heading-colour draw-text then
	dial-ink 0.8 dimmed to place-colour
	map-places ( place |
		place first landmark-ground to point
		frame point first point 2 @i map-at place second place-colour false draw-map-mark
	) each
	frame dial-ink draw-scale-bar
	map-left map-size + 16 - map-top 6 + "N" dial-ink draw-text
	map-left map-size + 12 - map-top 20 + map-left map-size + 12 - map-top 30 + dial-ink draw-segment ;

\ === the chart ===

\ the chart's paper: the water, the land in layers of height, from the coast at 0 through 250, 500, 1,000, 1,500, 2,000 and 3,000 ft (the bands and tints an estimate of a layer-coloured map of the time), the shores, rivers, railways, streets, the ten-mile squares and the printing
0xbcd6e4 constant chart-water-colour
[ 0 76 152 305 457 610 914 ] constant chart-band-heights
[ 0xc4d8a8 0xdce4b0 0xece0a8 0xe4c890 0xd4ac78 0xbc9068 0xa07858 ] constant chart-band-colours
0x3c5a78 constant chart-shore-colour
0x4878a8 constant chart-river-colour
0x302820 constant chart-ink
0x8a6a50 constant chart-street-colour
0x98a4a8 constant chart-square-colour
0xf4f0e0 constant chart-label-colour

\ the weights that take a line of a grid's corners to points among them: a matrix of a row for each point, a column for each corner, the point's place among the corners shared between the two corners either side of it
: corner-weights ( places n-corners -- weights )
	| places n-corners |
	places size n-corners 0-matrix to weights
	0 places size 1 do k
		places k @i to place
		place round-down 0 max2 n-corners 2 - min2 to lower
		place lower - 0 1 clamp to share
		weights 1 share - k lower !i,j drop
		weights share k lower 1+ !i,j drop
	loop
	weights ;

\ the land of one surveyed grid on the chart, tinted by height, a window pixel at a time: the grid's heights between its corners, by the weights each way, at the centre of every window pixel of the sheet the grid covers; each pixel the tint of the band its height reaches, the sea and the lochs, below 2 m, the water's; laid over the sheet as a picture
: draw-chart-grid ( frame grid -- )
	| frame grid |
	view-pixels to n
	sheet spread to sheet-height to sheet-width to sheet-top to sheet-left
	grid@west to west
	grid@south to south
	grid@spacing to spacing
	frame west south map-at to grid-bottom to grid-left
	frame west grid@columns 1- spacing * + south grid@rows 1- spacing * + map-at to grid-top to grid-right
	grid-left sheet-left max2 n * round-up to first-x
	grid-right sheet-left sheet-width + min2 n * round-down to last-x
	grid-top sheet-top max2 n * round-up to first-y
	grid-bottom sheet-top sheet-height + min2 n * round-down to last-y
	first-x last-x >= first-y last-y >= or if exit then
	sheet-left sheet-width 2 / + to centre-x
	sheet-top sheet-height 2 / + to centre-y
	[ first-x last-x 1 do x x 0.5 + n / centre-x - frame@scale / frame@x + west - spacing / loop ] to column-places
	[ first-y last-y 1 do y frame@z y 0.5 + n / centre-y - frame@scale / - south - spacing / loop ] to row-places
	column-places 1e9 ' min2 reduce round-down 0 max2 grid@columns 2 - min2 to first-column
	column-places -1e9 ' max2 reduce round-down 1+ grid@columns 1- min2 first-column 1+ max2 to last-column
	row-places 1e9 ' min2 reduce round-down 0 max2 grid@rows 2 - min2 to first-row
	row-places -1e9 ' max2 reduce round-down 1+ grid@rows 1- min2 first-row 1+ max2 to last-row
	grid@heights first-row last-row 1+ first-column last-column 1+ submatrix to block
	column-places ( place | place first-column - ) map last-column first-column - 1+ corner-weights to across
	row-places ( place | place first-row - ) map last-row first-row - 1+ corner-weights to down
	down block matmul across transpose matmul to fine
	fine 2 >= chart-band-colours first chart-water-colour - * chart-water-colour + to tints
	1 chart-band-heights size 1 do k
		fine chart-band-heights k @i >= chart-band-colours k @i chart-band-colours k 1- @i - * tints + to tints
	loop
	tints first-x first-y draw-view ;

\ a line of [ x z ] ground points on the chart
: draw-chart-line ( frame points colour -- )
	| frame points colour |
	points ( point | frame point first point second map-at 2 array ) map to places
	0 places size 1- 1 do k
		places k @i spread places k 1+ @i spread colour draw-segment
	loop ;

\ the airfields among the places on the chart, drawn as rings
[ :turnhouse :drem :abbotsinch :dalcross :acklington :wick :vaernes :bardufoss :dyce :montrose-air-station
  :castletown :hatston :skeabrae :sumburgh ] constant chart-airfields

\ the summits the chart marks with their heights in feet, from the map's heights
[ :ben-lomond :ben-cleuch :west-lomond :scald-law :tinto :earls-seat :arthurs-seat :north-berwick-law ] constant chart-summits

\ the chart on the pilot's knee across the whole sheet, the mission's own map in the detail of a printed one: the water, and over it the land of every surveyed grid tinted by height; the ten-mile squares; the coasts' and lochs' shores, the rivers, the cities' main-line railways and main streets; the summits with their heights in feet; the airfields as rings and the towns as dots with their names; the raid's target and the Tirpitz; the scale and north; the mission's name and how to put the chart away in a box at the top
: draw-chart-sheet ( mission frame -- )
	| mission frame ^placed-labels |
	sheet spread to sheet-height to sheet-width to sheet-top to sheet-left
	sheet-left sheet-top sheet-width sheet-height chart-water-colour fill-span
	terrain-grids ( grid | frame grid draw-chart-grid ) each
	16093.4 to square
	sheet-width 2 / frame@scale / to reach-x
	sheet-height 2 / frame@scale / to reach-z
	frame@x reach-x - square / round-down frame@x reach-x + square / round-up 1+ 1 do k
		frame k square * frame@z reach-z - map-at drop to column
		column sheet-top column sheet-top sheet-height + chart-square-colour draw-segment
	loop
	frame@z reach-z - square / round-down frame@z reach-z + square / round-up 1+ 1 do k
		frame frame@x k square * map-at to row drop
		sheet-left row sheet-left sheet-width + row chart-square-colour draw-segment
	loop
	frame map-lines ( segment | segment spread chart-shore-colour draw-segment ) each
	[ rivers@clyde rivers@forth rivers@kelvin ] rivers@ness concat ( course | frame course chart-river-colour draw-chart-line ) each
	[ glasgow-railways edinburgh-railways inverness-railways aberdeen-railways montrose-railways trondheim-railways narvik-railways ]
	( lines | lines ( line | frame line chart-ink draw-chart-line ) each ) each
	[ glasgow-streets edinburgh-streets inverness-streets aberdeen-streets peterhead-streets montrose-streets kirkwall-streets
	  lerwick-streets trondheim-streets ] ( streets | streets values ( line | frame line chart-street-colour draw-chart-line ) each ) each
	narvik-streets ( line | frame line chart-street-colour draw-chart-line ) each
	[ ] to placed-labels
	map-places ( place |
		place first to key
		key landmark-ground to point
		frame point first point 2 @i map-at to row to column
		column row 4 on-map? if
			chart-airfields key position-of 0 >= if
				column row 4 chart-ink draw-circle
				column row place second 7 false place-label to position
			else
				column 1 - row 1 - 3 3 chart-ink fill-span
				column row place second 5 false place-label to position
			then
			position null? not if position spread place second chart-ink draw-text then
		then
	) each
	chart-summits ( key |
		key landmark-ground to point
		frame point first point 2 @i map-at to row to column
		column row 4 on-map? if
			column 3 - row 2 + column 3 + row 2 + column row 3 - chart-ink fill-face
			key landmark-height 3.28084 * round "{0}" format to feet
			column row feet 5 false place-label to position
			position null? not if position spread feet chart-ink draw-text then
		then
	) each
	mission@raid to plan
	plan null? not if
		frame plan@target first plan@target 2 @i map-at "TARGET" raid-colour draw-map-cross
	then
	mission :aircraft :fighter @or :reconnaissance = if
		mission@target landmark-ground to place
		frame place first place 2 @i map-at "TIRPITZ" raid-colour draw-map-cross
	then
	frame chart-ink draw-scale-bar
	sheet-left sheet-width + 16 - sheet-top 34 + "N" chart-ink draw-text
	sheet-left sheet-width + 12 - sheet-top 48 + sheet-left sheet-width + 12 - sheet-top 58 + chart-ink draw-segment
	sheet-left sheet-top sheet-width 28 chart-label-colour fill-span
	sheet-left sheet-top 28 + sheet-left sheet-width + sheet-top 28 + chart-ink draw-segment
	sheet-left 8 + sheet-top 8 + mission@name chart-ink draw-text
	sheet-left sheet-width + 8 - "RELEASE N TO LOOK UP" text-width - sheet-top 8 + "RELEASE N TO LOOK UP" chart-ink draw-text ;

\ whether a mission may be flown in either fighter: every armed mission that does not fix its aircraft, but the flying lesson, which is the two-seat Spitfire's
: aircraft-choosable? ( mission -- flag )
	| mission |
	mission :aircraft :fighter @or :fighter = not if false exit then
	mission :lesson false @or mission :air-firing false @or not and not ;

\ the fighter a mission is flown in: the Hurricane where the mission fixes it, or where chosen and the mission allows the choice; otherwise the Spitfire
: flown-in ( mission choice -- kind )
	| mission choice |
	mission :aircraft :fighter @or :hurricane = if :hurricane exit then
	choice :hurricane = mission aircraft-choosable? and if :hurricane else :spitfire then ;

\ how many of a type, by the name the briefing gives it
: kind-plural ( kind -- text )
	| kind |
	kind :ju-88 = if "JU 88s" exit then
	kind :he-111 = if "HE 111s" exit then
	"BF 110s" ;

\ the particulars, each [ label value ], read from the mission and the aircraft chosen for it
: briefing-particulars ( mission choice -- rows )
	| mission choice |
	mission :moon null @or to moon
	mission@night if
		moon null? if "NIGHT, NO MOON" else moon second "NIGHT, THE MOON {0:.0f} DEG UP" format then
	else
		"DAY"
	then to time-text
	mission :aircraft :fighter @or :reconnaissance = if
		"SPITFIRE PR, UNARMED, SPLIT CAMERAS"
	else mission choice flown-in :hurricane = if
		"HURRICANE MK I, EIGHT BROWNINGS, 334 OR 287 ROUNDS EACH"
	else
		"SPITFIRE MK I, EIGHT BROWNINGS, 300 ROUNDS EACH"
	then then to aircraft-text
	mission@propeller :two-pitch = if "TWO-PITCH" else "CONSTANT-SPEED" then to propeller-text
	mission@emergency if "+6 LB, +12 LB EMERGENCY ON 100 OCTANE" else "+6 LB, 87 OCTANE" then to boost-text
	mission@start to start
	start 3 @i if
		"ON THE RUNWAY"
	else
		start 2 @i 2.23694 * start first second hundreds-of-feet "AIRBORNE, {0} FT, {1:.0f} MPH" format
	then to start-text
	mission@visibility clear-visibility >= if "CLEAR" else mission@visibility 1609.34 / "VISIBILITY {0:.1f} MILES" format then to visibility-text
	mission@cover 0 = if
		visibility-text ", NO CLOUD" +
	else
		mission@base hundreds-of-feet mission@cover 10 * round visibility-text "{0}, CUMULUS {1}/10 AT {2} FT" format
	then to weather-text
	mission@raid to plan
	plan null? if
		mission :aircraft :fighter @or :reconnaissance = if "HEAVY AND LIGHT FLAK ROUND THE FJORD"
		else mission :air-firing false @or if "NONE: A LYSANDER TUG AND ITS DROGUE"
		else "NONE" then then
	else
		plan@height hundreds-of-feet plan@kind kind-plural plan@n-vics 3 * "{0} {1} AT {2} FT" format
		mission :escort [ ] @or size to n-escort
		n-escort 0 > if n-escort ", {0} BF 110s ESCORTING" format + then
	then to opposition-text
	[ [ "TIME" time-text ] [ "AIRCRAFT" aircraft-text ] [ "PROPELLER" propeller-text ] [ "BOOST" boost-text ]
	  [ "START" start-text ] [ "WEATHER" weather-text ] [ "ENEMY" opposition-text ] ] to rows
	mission :wingmen [ ] @or size to n-wingmen
	n-wingmen 0 > if rows [ "SQUADRON" n-wingmen "{0} MORE SPITFIRES WITH YOU" format ] add-last! drop then
	rows ;

\ a model drawn turning about its vertical axis at an angle, seen from 9° above, nearly level so the canopy stands out against the background, without perspective: each point's place across the screen and up it, a scale's pixels a metre from a centre
: draw-model-turning ( model cx cy scale angle colour -- )
	| model cx cy scale angle colour |
	0.15 to tilt
	[ angle cos angle sin negate tilt sin *
	  0 tilt cos
	  angle sin angle cos tilt sin *
	  0 0 ] 4 2 matrix to turn
	model@points turn matmul to seen
	model@edges to edges
	0 edges size 2 do k
		edges k @i to i
		edges k 1+ @i to j
		cx seen i 0 @i,j scale * + cy seen i 1 @i,j scale * -
		cx seen j 0 @i,j scale * + cy seen j 1 @i,j scale * -
		colour draw-segment
	loop ;

\ the aircraft the mission is flown in, its undercarriage down, turning under the particulars in the space down to the briefing: the Hurricane when chosen and allowed, otherwise the Spitfire
: draw-chosen-aircraft ( mission choice top -- )
	| mission choice top |
	mission choice flown-in :hurricane = if models@hurricane-down 12.19 else models@spitfire-down 11.23 then to span to model
	briefing-top top - 8 - to room
	room 30 < if exit then
	290 span / room 4 / min2 to scale
	game :title-time 0 @or 0.4 * to angle
	model particulars-left 624 + 2 / top room 2 / + scale angle dial-ink draw-model-turning ;

\ the briefing screen: the mission's name, the map, the particulars, the briefing, and what the keys do, the choice of aircraft among them where the mission allows it
: draw-briefing ( mission frame segments choice -- )
	| mission frame segments choice |
	0 0 640 480 wall-colour fill-span
	320 12 mission@name 0xffffff centred-print
	mission frame segments true draw-briefing-map
	map-top 4 + to y
	mission choice briefing-particulars to rows
	0 rows size 1 do k
		rows k @i to row
		particulars-left y row first heading-colour draw-text
		row second values-width wrapped-lines to value-lines
		0 value-lines size 1 do m
			values-left y value-lines m @i dial-ink draw-text
			y 13 + to y
		loop
		y 4 + to y
	loop
	mission choice y draw-chosen-aircraft
	mission :briefing "" @or 640 32 - wrapped-lines to lines
	0 lines size 1 do k
		16 briefing-top k 13 * + lines k @i dial-ink draw-text
	loop
	mission aircraft-choosable? if
		320 448 "LEFT AND RIGHT: SPITFIRE OR HURRICANE" heading-colour centred-print
	then
	320 462 "RETURN OR START FLIES  -  ESCAPE FOR THE MISSIONS" 0xffffff centred-print ;
